# Project Rules

## Architecture

- Feature-first clean architecture: `presentation -> domain -> data`. Presentation calls usecases, usecases depend on domain repository contracts, data implements those contracts.
- Features isolated. No feature imports another feature's `data/` or `presentation/`.
- Use GetX for routing, DI, and controllers. Controllers hold UI state and call usecases; business rules belong in usecases, never widgets.
- Screens ≤ 200 lines; extract widgets, shared components, and helper methods.
- Never use widget methods (e.g. `Widget _buildFoo()`). Always extract reusable UI into a dedicated `StatelessWidget` or `StatefulWidget` class in its own file under the feature's `presentation/widgets/` folder.
- Domain entities live in `domain/entities/` (feature) or `shared/domain/entities/` (cross-feature).
- Data models in `data/models/` **extend** their matching domain entity.
- Models add serialization only: `fromJson`, `toJson`, and `toEntity()` / `toAuthSession()` when mapping to another aggregate.
- Presentation and usecases use entities only — never import `data/models/`.

## Colors

- Single color source of truth: `lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart`.
- Color constants named `c` + hex (e.g. `c987656` → `Color(0xFF987656)`).
- No raw `Color(...)`, `Colors.*`, or hex literals in feature pages/widgets.
- Semantic aliases allowed only inside `AppColors`, pointing to canonical `c` + hex constants.

## Assets

- PNG paths only in `lib/core/constants/png_asset.dart`.
- SVG paths only in `lib/core/constants/svg_asset.dart`.
- No hardcoded asset path strings in pages, controllers, or feature widgets.
- Military logo used for app logo, splash, and login via asset constants.
- Use `flutter_svg: ^2.3.0` for SVG rendering.

## Reusable Image Loading

- Use `lib/core/widgets/app_png_asset.dart` and `lib/core/widgets/app_svg_asset.dart`.
- `AppPngAsset` wraps `Image.asset`; accepts `width`, `height`, `fit`, `alignment`, `color`, `opacity`, `semanticLabel`, `cacheWidth`, `cacheHeight`.
- `AppSvgAsset` wraps `SvgPicture.asset`; accepts `width`, `height`, `fit`, `alignment`, `colorFilter`, `semanticsLabel`, and optional placeholder/error builders.
- Feature UIs use these wrappers — never call `Image.asset` or `SvgPicture.asset` directly.

## Typography

- Always use `Theme.of(context).textTheme` — never hardcode `TextStyle` inline.
- Font: Hind Siliguri. Declared once in `ThemeData`; all text inherits it.

## DRY

- No repeated logic. Extract shared code to utils, usecases, or base classes.
- Logic stays out of UI. Controllers and usecases own business rules; widgets only render and dispatch.

## Error Handling

- Wrap all business logic and controller calls in `try/catch`.
- UI shows only generic, user-friendly messages (e.g. `'Something went wrong. Please try again.'`).
- Detailed errors and stack traces go to the logger, never to the UI.

## Logging

- Use `logger` package (`^2.7.0`) for all console output.
- Log only in debug mode (`kDebugMode`).
- Never use `print`, `debugPrint`, or expose raw exceptions to users.
- **Always log API responses to the console** via `LoggingInterceptor` (`lib/core/network/interceptors/logging_interceptor.dart`). Route all HTTP traffic through `ApiClient` / Dio so request and response bodies are captured centrally.
- Sanitize secrets before logging (Authorization header, passwords, tokens). Never log raw credentials.

```dart
// ✅ GOOD
if (kDebugMode) logger.e('fetchExams failed', error: e, stackTrace: st);
showError('Something went wrong. Please try again.');

// ❌ BAD
print(e);
Text(e.toString());
```

## Naming

- Variables and functions: readable, descriptive, camelCase. No abbreviations unless universal (`id`, `url`).
- Booleans: prefix with `is`, `has`, `can` (e.g. `isLoading`, `hasError`).

## General

- Think before coding. Don't touch irrelevant files. Ask when intent is ambiguous.
